ChatGPT Response Notifier 0.7.0

This project uses the completion-monitoring implementation from ChatGPT Response Complete Notifier by Ram Haidar (ramhaidar/ChatGPT-Response-Complete-Notifier), revision cbe00dcfcff8a571f407c6109ed4d5f97cef60a9.

For version 0.7.0, extension/content-script.js remains byte-for-byte identical to the upstream file at that revision. The surrounding integration routes upstream completion events through a separate local terminal-status eligibility layer and then to this project's localhost Windows helper for persistent stacked notifications and managed updates without adding ChatGPT API polling. Only responses whose final non-whitespace line matches the GitHub work-session footer shape `[GITHUB_STATUS: UPPERCASE_CODE]` are notified or added to recent history. Refresh/reopen recovery uses the same footer rather than ChatGPT action-button UI. Response-preview data remains available in the notification/history backend while the compact light Windows toast renders the full browser-tab title and status code.

